      "message": "This does not work, because there is a std::recursive_mutex label_lock; nested inside the struct:\n\n```\nif/src/btif_rc.cc:2583:33: error: object of type \u0027btif_rc_device_cb_t\u0027 cannot be assigned because its copy assignment operator is implicitly deleted\nfloss-9999:  2583 |     btif_rc_cb.rc_multi_cb[idx] \u003d btif_rc_device_cb_t{};\nfloss-9999:       |                                 ^\nfloss-9999: ../../../../../../../tmp/portage/net-wireless/floss-9999/work/floss-9999/platform2/bt/system/btif/src/btif_rc.cc:220:24: note: copy assignment operator of \u0027btif_rc_device_cb_t\u0027 is implicitly deleted because field \u0027transaction_set\u0027 has a deleted copy assignment operator\nfloss-9999:   220 |   rc_transaction_set_t transaction_set;\nfloss-9999:       |                        ^\nfloss-9999: ../../../../../../../tmp/portage/net-wireless/floss-9999/work/floss-9999/platform2/bt/system/btif/src/btif_rc.cc:196:24: note: copy assignment operator of \u0027rc_transaction_set_t\u0027 is implicitly deleted because field \u0027label_lock\u0027 has a deleted copy assignment operator\nfloss-9999:   196 |   std::recursive_mutex label_lock;\nfloss-9999:       |                        ^\nfloss-9999: /usr/bin/../include/c++/v1/mutex:229:20: note: \u0027operator\u003d\u0027 has been explicitly marked deleted here\nfloss-9999:   229 |   recursive_mutex\u0026 operator\u003d(const recursive_mutex\u0026) \u003d delete;\nfloss-9999:       |                    ^\nfloss-9999: 1 error generated.\n```\n\nAny ideas how to fix this?\n\nPerhaps we can move that mutex to the top level struct rc_cb_t ? I\u0027m a bit anxious doing this change because it\u0027s more involved that just fixing the clang + glibc regression, perhaps it needs to be done separately from this CL.\n\nAlso btif_rc_cb.rc_multi_cb \u003d {}; does not work:\n\n```\nsystem/btif/src/btif_rc.cc:2587:26: error: array type \u0027btif_rc_device_cb_t[6]\u0027 is not assignable\nfloss-9999:  2587 |   btif_rc_cb.rc_multi_cb \u003d {};\nfloss-9999:       |   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ ^\nfloss-9999: 1 error generated.\n```\n\nFor this to work we would need to refactor the member to use something like: `std::array\u003cbtif_rc_device_cb_t, BTIF_RC_NUM_CONN\u003e rc_multi_cb;`\n\nwhich I feel is again out of scope for this cl...\n\nWDYT?",
